      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Venlafaxine is an antidepressant that selectively inhibits serotonin reuptake and is a norepinephrine inhibitor. Withdrawal syndromes can occur after abrupt drug discontinuation of long-term regimens."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "EXEGESIS",
          "content": "We report six cases of withdrawal symptoms after venlafaxine discontinuation."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Physicians must be aware of the frequency, rapidity and potent severity of these withdrawal syndromes."
        }
      ]},
